\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Error sources of Experiment~1, $\kappa =1$. (a)~Split identity: $\Gamma _S$ (real-space lattice sum) plus $\Gamma _L^{\rm  F}$ (mesh-free lattice Fourier sum, $k_c=2\xi \cdot 6.5$) against $\Gamma _{\rm  ref}$. The line is the pair-level error $\max _r|\theta _S+\theta _L-e^{-\kappa r}/r|/(e^{-\kappa r}/r)$. (b)~Real-space and (c)~Fourier truncation at $\xi =0.7$, with no other approximation present. The curves are the median over three seeds and the band is their range; dotted curves are cases A and B; the dashed curve is $e^{-x^2}$. (d)~Mesh error against the mesh-free lattice sum over the same modes at the production $k_c=5.74$, for uniform $N=128$, seed~1. The curves are the RMS over eight grid shifts, the bands the range over shifts, and the thin segments have slope $p$. (e)~Fitted slopes in $h$ on the four finest meshes with error $\ge 10^{-12}$. Filled markers use the production $k_c$; open markers use $k_c$ at $s=5.5$ (five configurations). (f)~Largest over RMS error across the eight grid shifts, for every mesh and $p$ of the eight-shift scans ($N\le 128$, production $k_c$).}}{8}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:exp1-components}{{1}{8}{}{}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces The production action $X\DOTSB \mapstochar \rightarrow \Gamma _hX$ against the dense full-periodic reference. (a)~Relative spectral error for the parameter sets accepted at $10^{-9}$, $10^{-7}$ and $10^{-5}$ on cases A and B. Filled markers are $N\le 128$ and open markers $N=256$. (b)~Absolute error against $\|\Gamma _{\rm  ref}\|_2$ at T7; the diagonal is relative $10^{-7}$; crosses are the box-length sets. (c)~Probe errors through the production matvec at T7. Translations are given as operator-normalized residuals; the dashed line is $10^{-7}$. (d)~Absolute error against box length at T7, at fixed $N=64$ (density varies) and at fixed density $n_A$ ($N$ varies). The realised $\eta $ is annotated.}}{9}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:exp1-action}{{2}{9}{}{}{}}
